v 3
d twinmatch: policy-twin selection by Mahalanobis distance
d
d twinmatch finds the comparison units that most resemble one
d treated unit -- its "policy twins" -- for small-N program
d evaluation: one district, county, campus, hospital, or firm
d adopted a policy, and the question is which untreated units
d look most like it.  It ranks every candidate by Mahalanobis
d distance (or Euclidean distance on z-scores) to the treated
d unit on stated covariates, optionally within strata and a
d caliper, and optionally on the outcome's pre-policy path
d (wide columns, or a long panel through time(), outcome(),
d and window()).  It reports the k nearest, a balance table of
d standardized differences, a support line, and a stability
d check that re-picks with each covariate removed; saving()
d writes the shortlist as a ledger file.  Twin ids and
d distances are returned in r().  It selects and describes;
d it does not weight twins or estimate effects, so it pairs
d with synth, scpi, sdid, and the DiD commands.  Deterministic.
d Requires Stata 16.0 or newer.  No dependencies.
d
d Author: Eric A. Booth, Sr Researcher, Texas 2036
d Support: eric.a.booth@gmail.com
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261114
d
f twinmatch.ado
f twinmatch.sthlp
